From: Artem Pelenitsyn <a.pelenitsyn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:58:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Present the base of mhs at its Hackage versions

The base of mhs is versioned like the compiler (base-0.16.9.0) and bundles
the modules of packages that are separate on Hackage: bytestring, text,
deepseq, stm, directory, process, hashable and integer-logarithms. A package
written for GHC depends on base-4.x and on those packages by name, so it
cannot be solved against what mhs provides: the only installed base is
0.16.9.0, and base is not reinstallable.

Describe the base of mhs the way MicroCabal does, with the versions from its
builtinPackages table ("totally fake; they are from GHC"): base at 4.19.1.0,
and the bundled packages as installed packages of their own, at the versions
MicroCabal gives them, depending on base, with the modules that are theirs
and no package file. The unit id of base stays base-0.16.9.0, which is also
the name of its package file, so the dependency closure of a component still
preloads the one base.pkg. A package file is now looked up under the unit id
first, then under the munged package id of a library built by Cabal, and a
package without library directories has nothing to load.

Tested with mhs 0.16.9.0: a library with 'base ^>=4.19, bytestring >=0.11'
and an executable with 'base >=4.14 && <5' solve, build and run, with only
base.pkg preloaded; the testsuite package has such bounds now.

